kokoro-espeak-ng is a Rust port of the text-to-phoneme part of eSpeak NG 1.52.0
(https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng, tag 1.52.0), and ships data compiled
from it. Like eSpeak NG, it is free software under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version; see LICENSE.

The ported C files carry these notices:

  Copyright (C) 2005 to 2015 by Jonathan Duddington
  Copyright (C) 2013-2017, 2020 Reece H. Dunn
  Copyright (C) 2021, 2022 Juho Hiltunen

Ported files: readclause.c, translate.c, translateword.c, dictionary.c,
numbers.c, tr_languages.c, langopts.c, phonemelist.c, and parts of voices.c,
encoding.c, common.c, phoneme.c and synthdata.c (src/libespeak-ng/).

src/ucd.rs and src/ucd_tables.rs come from ucd-tools, bundled with eSpeak NG
(src/ucd-tools/):

  Copyright (C) 2012-2018, 2021 Reece H. Dunn

ucd_tables.rs is generated by reference/espeak-ng-oracle/ucddump.c from
ucd-tools' tables, which are derived from the Unicode Character Database;
COPYING.UCD has the Unicode terms for that data.

Data (espeak-ng-data/)
----------------------

These are eSpeak NG 1.52 data files, unmodified, as bundled in the
espeakng-loader 0.2.4 Python package. Their sources are in the eSpeak NG
1.52.0 source release
(https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng/archive/refs/tags/1.52.0.tar.gz,
sha256 bb4338102ff3b49a81423da8a1a158b420124b055b60fa76cfb4b18677130a23):

  <lang>_dict      dictsource/<lang>_rules, <lang>_list, <lang>_extra,
                   <lang>_emoji (and <lang>_listx where present), compiled
                   with `espeak-ng --compile=<lang>`. ru_dict is built with
                   the extended word list dictsource/extra/ru_listx
                   (configure --with-extdict-ru).
  phontab,         phsource/ (phoneme definitions), compiled with
  phonindex        `espeak-ng --compile-phonemes`.
  lang/            espeak-ng-data/lang/ in the source release, as is.

Recompiling the dictionaries from that release (with
reference/espeak-ng-oracle's build of the library) reproduces every shipped
*_dict byte for byte, except ko_dict, whose rule groups come out in a
different order with the same contents. phontab and phonindex were not rebuilt.
